cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "leggedsnake: Leg mechanisms optimization using Python and genetic algorithms"
authors:
  - family-names: Farajallah
    given-names: Hugo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0769-4434"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, France"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-07-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HugoFara/leggedsnake"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/leggedsnake/"
url: "https://hugofara.github.io/leggedsnake/"
abstract: >-
  leggedsnake simulates and optimizes planar leg mechanisms using
  physics-based simulation, particle swarm optimization, and genetic
  algorithms. It builds on pylinkage's kinematic model to evolve
  walking linkages such as Jansen and Klann mechanisms.
keywords:
  - linkage
  - leg mechanism
  - optimization
  - walking linkage
  - genetic algorithms
  - particle swarm optimization
